# Stop working at night in Russian: aspect after перестать, успеть
subtitle: "Перестать работать, but успеть сделать: which aspect comes after which verb, as Tom and Masha write their New Year promises at «Кухонька»."
tags: ["russian","russian aspect","перестать","new year resolutions","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/aspect"]
thumb: "band \"Stop working at night in Russian\" stamp \"ПО НОЧАМ\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Two Russian autumn poems: Tyutchev and Bunin","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/210-russian-autumn-poems.cast"}

